/**
  MESSAGES array

  This is an associative array where the key is the message "code" and the data is the message content
  and the title for the message window.
  The last letter of the key is the language code: E for English, F for French.
  The first letter is M for message.  It would be possible to use other letter codes like E for error 
  messages or V for validation messages but that doesn't seem like it's needed at this time.
  The 5 digits are the unique number code of the message.  For ease of lookup and to avoid 
  duplication it would be wise to keep the numbers sequential.

  Up to 4 format specifiers ("%s") may be included in the message string as placeholders for values to
  be specified by the caller of the getMessage function.  For example, the message M00009E contains 2
  such specifiers: "An amount is required for Part %s Line %s".  The calling script could be
  CoreMessages.getMessage("M00009", "3", "27");
  This would place 3 and 27 in the message string in place of the first and second format specifiers
  respectively.

  To access the title portion of the data use CoreMessages.getTitle("M00009");

