//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//  MESSAGES array
//
//  This is an associative array where the key is the message "code" and the data is the message content
//	and the title for the message window.
// 	The last letter of the key is the language code: E for English, F for French.
//  The first letter is C for Custom message.
//	The 5 digits are the unique number code of the message.  For ease of lookup and to avoid 
//	duplication it would be wise to keep the numbers sequential.
//
//	Up to 4 format specifiers ("%s") may be included in the message string as placeholders for values to
//	be specified by the caller of the getMessage function.  For example, a message C00009E may contain 2
//	such specifiers: "Maximum %s characters.  Maximum amount should not be greater than %s.".  The 
//	calling script could be CoreMessages.getMessage("C00002", "3", "999");
//	This would place 3 and 99 in the message string so the message wouls read
//	"Maximum 3 characters.  Maximum amount should not be greater than 999."
//
//	To access the title portion of the data use CoreMessages.getTitle("C00002");
//
//  Last Modified: 
//		Apr 7, 2011 		PDI000			Initial version
//		Apr 21, 2011		PDI000			Modify the MESSAGES array to be multi-dimensional so that
//											the title of the messageBox is included
//		Jan 23, 2012		PDI000			Based on the new translation, modified the MESSAGES: C00001F, ..3F, ..4F, ..5F.
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

